From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Konstantin=20Sch=C3=B6ning?= <konstantin@lukianov.pp.ua>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] driver/stdio: treat a sent request as success, not as failure

The stdio APDU backend cannot work at all as written. json_request returns
what json_print returns, and json_print returns true when it has written the
message; every caller then treats that true as an error:

    if (json_request("connect", NULL, 0)) {
        return -1;
    }

So connect returns -1 the moment it succeeds in sending its request, and
euicc_init fails before a single reply is read. logic_channel_open and
transmit carry the same inversion, and would fail the same way if execution
ever reached them.

Confirmed on hardware rather than by reading: with a bridge answering
{"type":"apdu","payload":{"ecode":0}} to the connect request -- a valid,
well-formed success -- lpac still reported euicc_init failure and never
asked for a logical channel. The reply was not the problem; the request
having been sent was.

The HTTP stdio backend is unaffected: it ignores json_request's return
value entirely.

This matters here because this project builds no other APDU backend for the
bridge. lpac's native QMI and MBIM backends open the device themselves,
with no owner discovery, no lock and no bound, which is why they are not
built; the stdio backend is what lets the transport be arbitrated by code
that already does those things. Without this fix that backend is dead on
arrival and the bridge cannot exist.

No upstream pull request covers this.

--- a/driver/apdu/stdio.c
+++ b/driver/apdu/stdio.c
@@ -155,7 +155,7 @@ exit:
 static int apdu_interface_connect(struct euicc_ctx *ctx) {
     int ecode;
 
-    if (json_request("connect", NULL, 0)) {
+    if (!json_request("connect", NULL, 0)) {
         return -1;
     }
 
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@ static void apdu_interface_disconnect(struct euicc_ctx *ctx) {
 static int apdu_interface_logic_channel_open(struct euicc_ctx *ctx, const uint8_t *aid, uint8_t aid_len) {
     int ecode;
 
-    if (json_request("logic_channel_open", aid, aid_len)) {
+    if (!json_request("logic_channel_open", aid, aid_len)) {
         return -1;
     }
 
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ static int apdu_interface_transmit(struct euicc_ctx *ctx, uint8_t **rx, uint32_t
                                    uint32_t tx_len) {
     int ecode;
 
-    if (json_request("transmit", tx, tx_len)) {
+    if (!json_request("transmit", tx, tx_len)) {
         return -1;
     }
 
